# Provenance for itr_country_codes.csv
#
# Source: official ITR-2 Excel utility for AY 2025-26, sheet
# `DropDownValues`: the union of its three country named ranges
# `Country`, `Country_NoIndia` and `Country_Juridiction` (see Scope
# below). Each entry in those ranges has the form
# "{cbdt_code}-{COUNTRY_NAME_UPPERCASE}"; this CSV splits the two halves
# into separate columns and adds an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 lookup key.
#
# upstream-utility: ITR2_AY_25-26_V1.0
# upstream-utility-url: https://www.incometax.gov.in/iec/foportal/sites/default/files/2025-07/ITR2_AY_25-26_V1.0.zip
# upstream-utility-release-date: 2025-07-11
# extracted-at: 2026-05-16 (initial 26-country subset)
# expanded-at: 2026-05-30 (full 249-country union of all three named ranges under #74)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scope: this file lists 249 countries — the **union** of the three
# country named ranges in the source workbook:
#
#  * `Country` (sheet DropDownValues, cells BU3:BU251) — 247
#    countries. Used by Schedule FA Tables A1-G, Schedule TR,
#    Schedule CG buyer-country dropdowns, Schedule OS country
#    column, FSI residence-country column, and most other forms.
#  * `Country_NoIndia` (sheet DropDownValues, cells BW3:BW250) —
#    used by Schedule FA Table A2 (foreign custodial accounts:
#    excludes India because by definition an Indian custodial
#    account isn't on FA). Adds 2 countries that BU misses:
#    1013-WESTERN SAHARA and 260-ZAMBIA.
#  * `Country_Juridiction` (sheet DropDownValues, cells BY3:BY251)
#    — used by Schedule FSI jurisdiction-of-tax-residence column.
#    Includes the same WESTERN SAHARA + ZAMBIA additions as
#    Country_NoIndia.
#
# The union (249 entries) is taken so any IBKR-issued holding
# resolves at lookup time. **Caveat**: a row with iso_alpha2 = EH
# (Western Sahara) or ZM (Zambia) will resolve through the loader,
# but pasting the resulting "{cbdt_code}-{country_name_portal}"
# into Schedule FA Table A3 (whose dropdown is the smaller BU
# range) would be rejected by the portal. This is a CBDT data
# inconsistency, not an ibkr-fa bug — if a real user hits it the
# fix is at the CBDT portal end (or the user picks a different
# residence country with their CA's guidance).
#
# The expansion under #74 preserves the previously-vendored 26-country
# subset byte-for-byte: every existing iso_alpha2 row's cbdt_code,
# country_name, and country_name_portal are unchanged. Newly-added
# rows use ISO 3166-1's preferred current friendly-name where it
# differs from the CBDT portal form (e.g., Eswatini for SZ vs CBDT's
# legacy "SWAZILAND", North Macedonia for MK vs "MACEDONIA (THE FORMER
# YUGOSLAV REPUBLIC OF)"). The portal-facing country_name_portal column
# is always the verbatim UPPERCASE CBDT form so the f"{cbdt_code}-{
# country_name_portal}" assembly continues to match the portal's
# dropdown values exactly.
#
# Bug-fix history: this file previously listed
#   1 -> United Kingdom (WRONG; code 1 is Canada in the portal)
#   10 -> Netherlands (WRONG; the portal has no code 10; Netherlands is 31)
# Both were sourced from third-party practitioner blogs that conflated
# the CBDT codes with ISO numeric codes. Replaced with codes verified
# directly against the official ITR-2 utility.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Refresh process for a future AY:
#
# 1. Download the new ITR-2 utility zip from the official Downloads page
#    (https://www.incometax.gov.in/iec/foportal/downloads/income-tax-returns).
# 2. Unzip and open ITR2_AY_XX-XX_V1.X.xlsm with openpyxl (read_only,
#    keep_vba so the macro sheet loads). Read **all three** country
#    named ranges from the `DropDownValues` sheet:
#       * `Country`             (column BU, FA Tables A1-G + most forms)
#       * `Country_NoIndia`     (column BW, FA Table A2 — adds ZM + EH)
#       * `Country_Juridiction` (column BY, FSI jurisdiction picker)
#    Take the union (excluding the "(Select)" prompt, "9999-OTHERS"
#    fallback, and "9998-Not Applicable" sentinel). For AY 2025-26
#    the union is 249 distinct countries.
# 3. For each "{cbdt_code}-{NAME}" entry: split on the first "-",
#    look up an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 via pycountry, falling back to the
#    manual override map below (20 entries for CBDT names that
#    pycountry cannot auto-resolve due to portal-side quirks).
# 4. Diff the regenerated CSV against the current vendored one. Any
#    cbdt_code change (CBDT renumbering a country between AYs — rare
#    but possible) MUST be surfaced in the PR description and locked
#    by a regression test.
# 5. Update the `extracted-at` / `expanded-at` line of this provenance
#    file and the `upstream-utility-release-date`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manual override map (CBDT name → ISO 3166-1 alpha-2):
#
# These 20 entries are the CBDT portal names that pycountry's
# `countries.lookup()` cannot resolve. Each ISO code below was verified
# directly against the official ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 list (not derived
# algorithmically). Three failure modes:
#
#  * Accent / diacritic stripped:
#       REUNION                                       -> RE  (Réunion)
#       SAINT BARTHELEMY                              -> BL  (Saint Barthélemy)
#       COTE DIVOIRE                                  -> CI  (Côte d'Ivoire)
#       ALAND ISLANDS                                 -> AX  (Åland Islands)
#       CURACAO                                       -> CW  (Curaçao)
#
#  * Parenthesised long-form (CBDT lists the "official" UN form):
#       BOLIVIA (PLURINATIONAL STATE OF)              -> BO
#       CONGO (DEMOCRATIC REPUBLIC OF THE)            -> CD
#       IRAN (ISLAMIC REPUBLIC OF)                    -> IR
#       KOREA (DEMOCRATIC PEOPLES REPUBLIC OF)        -> KP
#       KOREA (REPUBLIC OF)                           -> KR
#       LAO PEOPLES DEMOCRATIC REPUBLIC               -> LA
#       MACEDONIA (THE FORMER YUGOSLAV REPUBLIC OF)   -> MK  (now "North Macedonia" in ISO)
#       MICRONESIA (FEDERATED STATES OF)              -> FM
#       VENEZUELA (BOLIVARIAN REPUBLIC OF)            -> VE
#       VIRGIN ISLANDS (BRITISH)                      -> VG
#       VIRGIN ISLANDS (U.S.)                         -> VI
#
#  * Politically-outdated or short-form synonym:
#       HOLY SEE                                      -> VA  (Vatican City State)
#       SWAZILAND                                     -> SZ  (now Eswatini in ISO 2018)
#       TIMOR-LESTE(EAST TIMOR)                       -> TL  (note missing space)
#       TURKEY                                        -> TR  (ISO renamed to Türkiye 2022)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Columns:
#
# iso_alpha2          ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code (e.g., "US").
#                     Used as the lookup key from IBKR's
#                     IssuerCountryCode field.
# cbdt_code           Numeric code as shown in the portal dropdown
#                     (e.g., "2" for United States). Note these are
#                     mostly E.164 country calling codes — but not
#                     always (Canada is "1", USA is "2", etc.), so
#                     do NOT derive these algorithmically.
# country_name        Title-case country name suitable for the audit
#                     section of the review CSV (less shouty than the
#                     UPPERCASE portal form).
# country_name_portal Verbatim UPPERCASE country name as it appears
#                     in the portal dropdown. The portal-facing
#                     Country column on Schedule FA Table A3 is
#                     formed as f"{cbdt_code}-{country_name_portal}",
#                     e.g., "2-UNITED STATES OF AMERICA".
